<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hanbo honorary chairman to appeal.</title>
<headline>Hanbo honorary chairman to appeal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The honorary chairman of the Hanbo Group, Chung Tae-soo, will appeal a two-year jail sentence handed down by a Seoul court for bribing former president Roh Tae-woo, a group spokesman said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;We are not sure when we would appeal but our lawyers are preparing it,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Chung was among nine businessmen found guilty on Monday by the Seoul District Criminal Court for bribery.</p>
<p>All the businessmen have seven days to lodge appeals of their sentences. During that time they remain free.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
